==Trivia==
*Although it sounds similar to ''loser'', the name Luza (ルーザ ''Rūza'') is most likely derived from the Japanese word for monkey (猿 ''saru''), which becomes ''zaru'' in certain compound words due to ''[[wikipedia:Rendaku|rendaku]]''.
**The "Zero" in Zero Luza's name could be foreshadowing [[Zero Legends]]. This connection is strengthened by the fact that the initials of Zero Luza and Zero Legends are both ZL, and by [[Ancient Egg: N000 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N000]] evolving into Ape Lord Luza.
*Since its [[Great Ape Luza|prior form]] is a [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]], Zero Luza may have been inspired by ''Monster Hunter Rise: Sunbreak''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s [[wikia:monsterhunter:Garangolm|Garangolm]], a huge, grey-and-green gorilla-like monster associated with nature. Other parallels between Zero Luza and Garangolm include heavily armored arms, eye color when attacking (red), and becoming more dangerous as their health drops.
*Zero Luza is the only [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] enemy whose "core" is green rather than black and the only one whose Japanese description does not mention genome modification nor the [[Laboratory of Relics]].
**This could mean Zero Luza is the first natural Colossus enemy, since the color green is often associated with nature and [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relics]].
*Zero Luza can be seen as a foil to [[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|True Superfeline]], [[Raging Bahamut Cat]], [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|enemy Mecha-Bun]] and [[Relic Bun-Bun]].
**True Superfeline:
***True Superfeline is a fast, small embodiment of [[Humanity Catified]] whose Japanese description says it appears at the end of [[wikipedia:Eternal return|eternal return]], while Zero Luza is a slow, towering ancestor of humanity encountered in the ancient past, just after Humanity Catified.
***Superfeline II shrinks when it evolves into True Superfeline, whereas Great Ape Luza becomes much larger as Zero Luza.
***True Superfeline's abilities directly counter Zero Luza's Relic/Colossus typing.
***True Superfeline is the last unit of the first rarity ([[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]]), obtainable only after clearing the last chapter of [[Cats of the Cosmos]], while Zero Luza is the final boss of [[Uncanny Legends]], which has "origin" as a common theme.
***Their Japanese names both contain the word ''chō'' (超, "super"). True Superfeline is Neko Chōjin (ネコ超人, "Cat Superman" or "Cat Superhuman"), while Zero Luza is Chō Seimeitai Zero Rūza (超生命体ゼロルーザ, "[[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Super-Lifeform]] Zero Luza").
***The last kanji in True Superfeline's Japanese name is 人 ("person", "human" or "an individual"), which is also present in the Japanese names of Humanity Catified, [[Reign of the Ape Lord]], [[Ape Lord's Revenge]] and [[Birth of True Man]].
***True Superfeline's previous form is named Superfeline II, while Zero Luza has the number zero in its name.
***Both were added in [[Version 12.0 Update|Version 12.0]].
**Raging Bahamut Cat:
***Raging Bahamut Cat is an ancient weapon who ended the world once, while Zero Luza is an ancient guardian of the [[Sacred Forest]] and is associated with origin.
***Raging Bahamut Cat is [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] after taking the costume that shackled his power off of his body, while Zero Luza is Great Ape Luza after taking energy said to be the origin of all things into its body and awakening its true power.
***Bahamut Cat shrinks and moves faster after becoming Raging Bahamut Cat, whereas Great Ape Luza becomes larger and slower as Zero Luza.
***Raging Bahamut Cat is the final boss of the second set of [[Main Chapters Levels|Main Chapters]], [[Into the Future]], while Zero Luza is the final boss of the second set of Legend Stages sub-chapters, Uncanny Legends.
***Both are dual-type enemies with the traits introduced at the beginning of their respective campaigns. Raging Bahamut Cat is [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]]/[[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]], while Zero Luza is Relic/Colossus.
***Instead of the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon]], the 48th stage of [[Empire of Cats]] in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]] is [[wikipedia:Iriomote Island|Iriomote Island]], which unlocks Bahamut Cat in Chapter 3. The [[Media:Rc164.png|tree]] that serves as the enemy base in all three of Great Ape Luza's stages may reference the [[Media:Ec047 ja.png|tree]] from Iriomote Island, as the phrase 野生の底力 ''yasei no sokojikara'' ("underlying power of the wild") on Iriomote Island's base is also present in the Japanese description of [[Wild Doge]], who appears in Ape Lord's Revenge, Birth of True Man and Revival of Origin. Furthermore, ''[[wikipedia:Awamori|awamori]]'', the drink mentioned in Wild Doge's Japanese description, is a signature product of [[wikipedia:Okinawa Prefecture|Okinawa]], the Japanese prefecture where Iriomote Island is located.
***Raging Bahamut Cat appears in the 48th stage of Into the Future, Bahamut Cat drops from the 48th stage of Empire of Cats, and Great Ape Luza appears in the 48th sub-chapter of Uncanny Legends.
**Mecha-Bun and Relic Bun-Bun:
***Enemy Mecha-Bun's Japanese name contains the Greek letter Ω ([[wikipedia:Omega|omega]]), which is the twenty-fourth and last letter of the Greek alphabet and often used to denote the end, the final part, or the limit of something. By contrast, Zero Luza is associated with origin.
***Enemy Mecha-Bun, Relic Bun-Bun and Zero Luza all have Omni Strike and attack with their fists.
***[[Mecha-Bun (Special Cat)|Allied Mecha-Bun]]'s description refers to it as an ancient superweapon, while Relic Bun-Bun and Zero Luza are ancient guardians.
***Mecha-Bun is the final boss of Stories of Legend, Relic Bun-Bun is the first boss of Uncanny Legends, and Zero Luza is the final boss of Uncanny Legends.
***Both Relic Bun-Bun and Zero Luza are variants of the bosses preceding them. Relic Bun-Bun is a variant of Mecha-Bun, while Zero Luza is a variant of Great Ape Luza.
***Both Relic Bun-Bun and Zero Luza attack "mercilessly" (though their Japanese descriptions use different words for "merciless": 容赦なく ''yōshanaku'' and 無慈悲 ''mujihi'', respectively).
*Zero Luza's Japanese description stating that it took in energy said to be the '''origin''' (起源) of all things and '''awakened''' (覚醒) its true power is a reference to [[Revival of Origin]]'s Japanese name, '''Awakening of Origin''' (起源の覚醒).
*Zero Luza has the highest attack power and money drop of all Relics and the highest attack power and DPS, longest attack foreswing and longest attack cycle of all Colossus enemies.

